us states ballistic shield health is  increased by 57 percent for every 30,000  stamina you could try for 9k stamina to  get the maximum out of this bonus but  you'd actually end up with less shield  health duty of skill power being quite  low so for this reason I'd recommend  aiming for 6 case stamina and putting  everything else into electronics in  skill power the other advantage to this  is that your second skill the support  station will come back faster and last  longer and you'll find this quite  important when running the resistance  skill power has been rolled onto the  kneepads and backpack with more skill  haste onto the chest and holster  enemy armor damage into the chest mask  and gloves and damage to elites onto the  mask and kneepads as per usual ammo  capacity has been rolled onto the chest  and backpack this is particularly  important with this build as you'll go  through a lot of Emma  as per the d3 set requirements you'll  need a good SMG I'd recommend the house  if you have one but an mp5 or org with  the right talents will do the job here  I'm using the mp5 St mine isn't the best  example as it has most of this talent  slot but I've used this to show that the  house isn't required in order for this  build to be successful some of the wit  and talents to aim for are destructive  for extra damage predatory to help keep  that constant flow of health  replenishment and responsive in the  third slot this is another good boost to  your damage particularly useful with  this build as most of your fighting will  be up close I recommend that your  secondary weapon is something with a bit  more range you'll only be using it four  times when you're dropping back into  cover to allow your shield to recharge  or if you're trying to conserve your SMG  mo in this example I'm using a  lightweight infall with destructive  predatory and determined so in this case  I'm also using it as a way to keep my  signature skills off cooldown  obviously the ballistic shield 